#UD The data in this file are valid in the energy range 1.0 keV to 100 MeV
#UD for the elements Z = 1 - 100.
#UD
#UD Column description (in brackets, the corresponding label in the published tables):
#UD 1:PhotonEnergy[MeV]
#UD 2:MassAttenuation[cm^2/g]
#UD 3:TotalCrossSection[barn/atom] (Mass Attenuation)
#UD
#UD The column 1,2 are copied from the above reference. The column 3
#UD is been calculated from columns 2 for consistency with
#UD other DABAX cross section tables and related applications. The formula used is
#UD col3 = col2 / cf
#UD cf = 1e-24*AVOGADRO/AtomicMass 
#UD For info, the keyword #UCONV contains the used numerical value 1/cf for each Z
#UD For the absorption edges, the energy value is duplicated (before and after the jump)
